# shellcheck shell=bash
#
# betanet — ecash-com/bitcoin @ betanet-bridge.
#
#   https://github.com/ecash-com/bitcoin/tree/betanet-bridge
#
# The SUCCESSOR to alphanet, and a DIFFERENT network from it: different fork
# height, different magic bytes, and — the one that bites — a different
# OP_DRIVECHAIN opcode. Every value below was read out of the branch's own
# source and out of the enforcer's `betanet` preset on 2026-09-16, so they
# match what the binaries will actually do.
#
# THE FORK HAS NOT HAPPENED YET. EcashHeight is 967,680 and mainnet is a few
# hundred blocks short of it (fork expected ~2026-09-20). Below that height
# this chain IS plain Bitcoin history, so a node has to sync ~967k real blocks
# before it can mine block one of the fork.

PROFILE_DESC=${PROFILE_DESC:-"betanet forknet — mainnet fork at block 967,680 (bridge branch)"}

# --- mainchain -------------------------------------------------------------
BITCOIN_REPO=${BITCOIN_REPO:-https://github.com/ecash-com/bitcoin.git}
BITCOIN_REF=${BITCOIN_REF:-betanet-bridge}
BITCOIN_PIN=${BITCOIN_PIN:-d7831c0af6}            # "Implement BTC -> ECX P2P bridge", 2026-08-06
#
# RE-CHECK THIS PIN BEFORE THE FORK. The branch still carries pre-fork
# consensus parameters that can move until 967,680 is mined — in particular
# EcashForkBits (chainparams.cpp), currently 0x19044b7e, i.e. difficulty 1e9
# at the fork block. A node pinned to a stale value forks itself off at the
# first block. `git log --oneline <pin>..origin/betanet-bridge -- src/kernel/`
# before treating this as final.

# betanet-bridge compiles BITCOIN_CONF_FILENAME as ecash.conf — same name as
# alphanet-bridge, NOT drivechain-ecash.conf (drynet3). A file under any other
# name is read by nothing and bitcoind comes up on stock defaults.
BTC_CONF_NAME=${BTC_CONF_NAME:-ecash.conf}
BTC_DATADIR_NAME=${BTC_DATADIR_NAME:-betanet}

# Same default ports as alphanet-bridge: RPC 8532, P2P 8533 (mainnet-role
# chain). That means a box running BOTH alphanet and betanet must set
# SVC_SUFFIX and move one of them — they collide exactly.
BTC_RPC_PORT=${BTC_RPC_PORT:-8532}
BTC_P2P_PORT=${BTC_P2P_PORT:-8533}
# eca5b104. alphanet is eca5a104 — ONE NIBBLE apart, and it is the nibble that
# decides which network you are on. Betanet's testnet/signet/regtest variants
# are eca5b114 / eca5b124 / eca5b134.
BTC_NETWORK_MAGIC=${BTC_NETWORK_MAGIC:-eca5b104}

# The branch ships four DNS seeds (chainparams.cpp): seed.beta.ecash.ninja,
# seed.beta.bip300.xyz, seed.beta.ecash.drivecha.in, seed.beta.ecash.zuexeuz.net.
# As of 2026-09-16 only ecash.ninja (37.27.102.58) and zuexeuz.net
# (198.57.27.71) resolve, and drivecha.in does not resolve at all — so the seed
# set is thin and handing bitcoind a known-good peer is worth doing.
BTC_ADDNODE=${BTC_ADDNODE:-37.27.102.58:8533}

# --- enforcer --------------------------------------------------------------
# The `betanet` preset landed on master and is NOT in any release, so this
# profile must track master. It carries, from lib/types.rs:
#   bip300_activation_height 967,680   network_magic eca5b104
#   datadir_suffix "betanet"           op_drivechain OP_NOP8 (0xb7)
#   thresholds BETANET = MAINNET but unused-slot activation at 1008 (51%)
#
# OP_NOP8 IS THE ONE THAT MATTERS. Every build up to alphanet put
# OP_DRIVECHAIN on OP_NOP5 (0xb4); betanet moved it to OP_NOP8 (0xb7). Run
# this network under the alphanet preset and the enforcer parses no BIP300
# messages at all — it does not error, it just sees an empty drivechain.
ENFORCER_REPO=${ENFORCER_REPO:-https://github.com/LayerTwo-Labs/bip300301_enforcer}
ENFORCER_REF=${ENFORCER_REF:-master}
ENFORCER_PIN=${ENFORCER_PIN:-b0acff3}             # "Fix flaky gh attestation verify check", 2026-09-16
ENFORCER_NETWORK_PRESET=${ENFORCER_NETWORK_PRESET:-betanet}
# Empty: the preset already carries eca5b104. Setting it here would only let
# the two disagree.
ENFORCER_NETWORK_MAGIC=${ENFORCER_NETWORK_MAGIC:-}

# --- thunder (sidechain 9) -------------------------------------------------
# Not required for a pool node — kept here so the profile stays complete and a
# later betanet node can bring the sidechain up without re-deriving this.
#
# thunder-rust master (aef21e7) has NO betanet network: the enum is
# regtest/signet/forknet/alphanet only (lib/net/peer/message.rs:19), and the
# magic is "THNDR" in Baudot-Murray with the network id in the low bits of
# byte 4 — 00 regtest / 01 signet / 02 forknet / 03 alphanet.
#
# So an override IS required here, unlike on alphanet where one was wrong:
# plain `--network forknet` gives magic 85189502 AND dials the forknet seeds
# (explorer.bip300.xyz, 157.180.8.224), which run a DIFFERENT mainchain
# underneath. 85189504 continues upstream's own numbering with the next free
# id. Revisit the moment upstream adds Network::Betanet — if they pick a
# different byte, this has to follow it or the node is alone.
THUNDER_REPO=${THUNDER_REPO:-https://github.com/LayerTwo-Labs/thunder-rust.git}
THUNDER_REF=${THUNDER_REF:-master}
THUNDER_PIN=${THUNDER_PIN:-aef21e7}               # "Move to new block producer RPC for withdrawal bundles", 2026-09-10
THUNDER_NETWORK=${THUNDER_NETWORK:-forknet}
THUNDER_NETWORK_MAGIC=${THUNDER_NETWORK_MAGIC:-85189504}
THUNDER_DATADIR_NAME=${THUNDER_DATADIR_NAME:-thunder-betanet}
SIDECHAIN_ID=${SIDECHAIN_ID:-9}
THUNDER_PEER=${THUNDER_PEER:-}

# --- assumeutxo ------------------------------------------------------------
# betanet-bridge carries the STOCK Bitcoin Core mainnet snapshot entries —
# 840,000 and 880,000 — because everything below the fork is real mainnet
# history. 880,000 is the useful one and a stock Core mainnet snapshot at that
# height is loadable here.
#
# No URL: data.drivechain.dev serves drynet3 only (and 404s at the root as of
# 2026-09-16). Point SNAPSHOT_FROM at a node you already run, or leave this
# empty and sync from the seeds.
SNAPSHOT_HEIGHT=${SNAPSHOT_HEIGHT:-880000}
SNAPSHOT_URL=${SNAPSHOT_URL:-}
SNAPSHOT_BYTES=${SNAPSHOT_BYTES:-}

MIN_DISK_GB=${MIN_DISK_GB:-950}
